-- title:
--   Theorem 3: decomposition into exchange, finite, and l-body phase factors
-- statement:
--   Use the physical register $\mathcal H_n=(\mathbb C^2)^{\otimes n}$. Rotational invariance means commuting with $U^{\otimes n}$ for every one-qubit unitary $U$. The legal spins are $j=n/2-r$, $r=0,\ldots,\lfloor n/2\rfloor$, and $\Pi_j$ is the actual spectral projector of $J^2$ at $j(j+1)$. Write $R_{ab}=(X_aX_b+Y_aY_b+Z_aZ_b)/2$ and $\mathcal V_k,\mathfrak v_k$ for the group of finite compositions of $k$-local invariant gates and its generated real Lie algebra, including scalar phases. Exchange-only circuits contain finite products of $e^{-itR_{ab}}$ with real $t$. Set $C_0=I$ and, for even $l>0$, $C_l=(l/2)!^{-1}\sum_{i_1,\ldots,i_l\ \mathrm{distinct}}R_{i_1i_2}\cdots R_{i_{l-1}i_l}$. Extend $C_l=0$ above $2\lfloor n/2\rfloor$. Its sector eigenvalue is $c_l(j)=\operatorname{Tr}(C_l\Pi_j)/\operatorname{Tr}(\Pi_j)$. All body-index sums below are over even indices.
--
--   For the physical even indices define $D_l=C_l/\operatorname{Tr}(C_l^2)$, and let $G_0$ be the subgroup generated by $\exp(i2\pi D_l)$ and $\exp(i2\pi\Pi_j/\operatorname{Tr}\Pi_j)$ for all legal $j$ and all physical even $l$. It is finite and abelian and depends only on $n$. Every invariant unitary $V$ has
--   $$V=\widetilde V V_0\prod_l\exp(i\phi_lD_l),\qquad \widetilde V\in S\mathcal V_2,\quad V_0\in G_0,$$
--   where $\phi_l\in(-\pi,\pi]$ represents $\Phi_l(V)$. The three factors commute pairwise, and $\widetilde V$ is exchange-realizable. No uniqueness is claimed. The full even generator range corrects G17 in accordance with G32–G33.
-- source:
--   Rotationally-Invariant Circuits: Universality with the exchange interaction and two ancilla qubits, arXiv:2202.01963v1, PDF p. 26, Theorem 3: decomposition into exchange, finite, and l-body phase factors

